A||||3||drednot||Temp- 220  normal?||||5||
Z||000000||drednot||05-21-2001||07:49 PM||||Is a temp of 220 normal for a fiero?  Mine runs at that temp just about all the time.  when I am sitting in traffic, it gets up to 240+ and the temp light comes on.  it has never gottem in the red though.  is this normal?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||05-21-2001||08:10 PM||||I don't think that it is normal to be running at 220.  The fan should be kicking on before the temperature light comes on.  Thermostat(?), fan switch(?), radiator got crud in it (?), cooling lines crushed (?), waterpump not pumping (?)<P>My cars run at 180-190, fan kicks on at 220, the temperature drops right back down.||||reg||3
Z||000002||thomas_l||05-21-2001||08:26 PM||||You ought to get a coolant thermometer and check to see if your gauge/sender is accurate. My 87 GT has the OEM switches and the gauge agrees: <P>cruising 195<BR>traffic 230 fan turns on, 220 fan turns off||||reg||1
Z||000003||KissMySSFiero||05-21-2001||09:44 PM||||quick diagnostic for this.  when its hot, run your hand across the radiator.  if the temp is not consistant across the radiator then you have crud in there.  before you pull it i would try to get a flush chemical and run it thru.  do it just as it says on the container too.  if that doesnt fix it then you will most likely have to pull the rad.  i had to do this a few weeks ago.  i thought i was crud in there so i pulled the rad and removed the side tanks.  well there wasnt crud,  it was just corroded and all it needed was to be flush.  i didnt have new o rings for is so now it leaks.  ive just been too lazy to finish it right.  its easier to just do it right the first time.  good luck hope this helped.<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>      <P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">          <BR>"When in Doubt..Whip it out!!"||||reg||1
